WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.618
Hi! In an open cloze, there are no options. You think of one word for each ___ yourself. It sounds hard, but most answers are common little words.

2
00:00:12.768 --> 00:00:21.642
First read the whole passage. ___ one: Mei is very interested ___ insects. We say interested in, so the answer is in.

3
00:00:21.792 --> 00:00:29.778
___ two: She was curious, ___ she joined the nature club. The second part is a result, so the answer is so.

4
00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:39.834
___ three: a park ___ has a butterfly garden. We need a word that refers back to the park and joins the description, so the answer is which or that.

5
00:00:39.984 --> 00:00:48.042
___ four: ___ butterflies there were colourful. These are the particular butterflies in that garden, so the answer is The.

6
00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:53.730
When you've finished, read it all again to check the meaning and grammar.

7
00:00:53.880 --> 00:01:01.914
Open cloze often tests five kinds of small words. First, prepositions, like in, on, at, of and for.

8
00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:05.274
Second, articles: a, an and the.

9
00:01:05.424 --> 00:01:10.386
Third, pronouns, like he, it and their, and also which and who.

10
00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:19.578
Fourth, conjunctions, like and, but, so and because. Fifth, helping verbs, like is, was, has, had and did.

11
00:01:19.728 --> 00:01:25.410
Watch out! Some pupils write two words in one blank, and that loses marks!

12
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:31.818
In an open cloze, each ___ takes only one word, and it must be spelt correctly.

13
00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:38.106
After filling it in, read the whole sentence to check the meaning and grammar.

14
00:01:38.256 --> 00:01:48.858
Your turn! It was raining heavily, ___ we stayed indoors. Fill in one word. Pause and think.

15
00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:55.650
The answer is so, because staying indoors is the result. Did you get it right?

16
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:06.210
Another one! My little brother is afraid ___ thunder. Fill in one word. Pause and think.

17
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:11.514
The answer is of: afraid of. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:22.578
Here's another! The boys ___ playing football when it started to rain. Fill in one word. Pause and think.

19
00:02:22.728 --> 00:02:32.970
The answer is were. For an action in progress in the past, we use were plus ing, and the boys is plural. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:42.810
One more! ___ you like to join us for lunch? Fill in one word. Pause and think.

21
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:50.466
The answer is Would. Would you like is a polite way to invite someone. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:50.616 --> 00:03:04.434
Remember: read the whole passage, look around each ___ and think whether it needs a preposition, article, pronoun, conjunction or helping verb. One word per ___, spelt correctly, and read it all again.

23
00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:09.426
Next time you read, notice these little words!

